# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets. Nothing in this block may ever be committed.
# The repository becomes PUBLIC at submission; a secret committed once is a
# secret leaked permanently, because git history survives deletion.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
!ops/**/*.example.crt
secrets/
*secrets*.json
.aws/
credentials
# The shapes a repository of this kind grows. ops/41_RUNBOOK.md section 2.5 and
# settings.py both say the shell exports the environment, which is precisely the
# direnv use case, so .envrc is the most likely next credential file here.
# ops/gate-env.sh advertises itself as "committed and contains no secret", which
# invites a *.local.sh sibling that is not. (D-00-005.)
.envrc
.netrc
.npmrc
.pypirc
*.local.sh
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
id_rsa*
*.tfvars

# Probe transcripts are committed ON PURPOSE (they are gate evidence), but only
# after tools/scrub.py has masked credentials, ARNs and account ids. A raw,
# unscrubbed transcript must never land.
ops/**/*.raw.txt

# T0.2 names this entry and 22_EVAL_DATASETS.md section 1.4 says reports/ is
# "git-ignored except the pinned baseline". Without it, every generated eval
# report would be committed. (D-00-005.)
evals/reports/*.json
!evals/reports/baseline.json
ops/**/*.unscrubbed.txt

